// HOLE 1 — a plural std/store's rows cannot be iterated ON DEMAND.
//
// `std/store:query` is the only row-iteration primitive, and it is a
// top-level-only comptime transform: it resolves its store by scanning
// TOP-LEVEL program items. Nested inside a repeatable handler/loop body (here a
// `! each` for-loop; equally a vaxis `! draw` / `! key` handler) it fails to
// resolve the store — even though `items` is declared `capacity: 8` right above.
//
// This blocks the retained-mode render a TUI needs: repainting all current rows
// on a NON-mutating event (a selection-highlight change, a resize repaint, a
// manual refresh). The store is reactive-incremental by design ("No
// reconciliation pass, no scan: the aggregate rides the write paths" —
// koru/tests/regression/600_STDLIB/690_STORE/690_041_store_arena_live_hp_aggregate),
// so there is deliberately no on-demand scan — but a retained-mode renderer
// (vaxis) needs exactly that.
//
// EXPECTED: prints `v 10` / `v 20` on each of the 2 iterations (rows swept on
//   demand), OR a clear koru-level diagnostic naming the real constraint.
// ACTUAL:   BACKEND_COMPILE_ERROR — "std/store:query(items): unknown store - no
//   std/store:new(items) found" — which is ALSO misleading: the store IS
//   declared; the real constraint is "query cannot be nested in a handler body".

~import std/io
~import std/store

~std/store:new(items, capacity: 8) { v: i64 }
~std/store:insert(items) { v: 10 }
~std/store:insert(items) { v: 20 }

~for(0..2)
! each _ |> std/store:query(items)
    ! query { entity.v } |> std/io:print.ln("v {{ v:d }}")
